  "body": "The review of PR #3709 found no blocker. These items stay open:\n\n- [ ] `xtask/src/quick_subs.rs:26` reads a submodule with no `pub` item as private. An `impl Trait for Type` in that submodule is visible to the other submodules. The filter `<sub>::` can then miss a test in another submodule. Add `impl ... for` to the `shared` rule (the whole suite runs).\n- [ ] The rule `^\\s*pub\\b` misses an attribute and `pub` on one line (`#[allow(dead_code)] pub fn`).\n- [ ] `braces::code` has no direct unit test. Add a table test: raw strings, `cr\"...\"`, nested block comments, `'\"'`, `'\\''`, lifetimes, byte strings. An error that hides a `mod` token makes the guard of the heavy filter weaker.\n- [ ] The loop variable `whole` in `quick_checks_old_and_new_hunk_sides_without_widening_in_test_edits` now means \"outside the test fns\". Rename it.\n- [ ] No run of a real `<sub>::` step is pinned; the tests read the plan text only.\n\nA miss of the quick tier is found by the post-merge batch tier, which runs whole suites.\n\nRefs #3706.\n",
